From daf8106ea421cd52b24a52a79b03800c4390c486 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 15:42:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/14] fix(trace): Edge Detection previews as the outlines it
 engraves (ADR-396)

Edge Detection results engrave as lines: a Line operation for vectors
and Outlines for raster scan (ADR-235 section 2). The preview, Overlay
and Multi-File Trace SVGs filled them as solid shapes, so the operator
saw filled letters that would burn only as outlines. They are now drawn
as strokes, like Centerline, and preview strokes stay one screen pixel
wide at any zoom so thin outlines on a large trace grid stay visible.

The style label no longer calls Edge Detection and the filled presets
both "Closed outlines": filled presets say "Filled shapes", Edge
Detection says "Outline paths". The Result hint says what each result
engraves as (Fill operation, Line operation, or thin raster lines).

Expectation updated in ImportImageDialog.workflow.test.ts: the filled
vector hint now reads "Editable filled shapes, engraved with a Fill
operation." because the old text offered line operations for fills.
The Edge case in paths-to-svg-centerline.test.ts now expects strokes.
Dialog state helpers moved to trace-dialog-state.ts so DialogBody stays
under the function-size cap.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
